# release.scenario with uart's burst capped at 1 and root's flood (M9;
# docs/design.md, "Network scenarios" and "The M9 Hyper-V check"): what the
# Hyper-V check's release-burst1 image boots, on QEMU. The kernel command
# line's uart.burst=1, which root reads, says so in its summary and passes
# to uart in rdi at spawn, so uart writes one byte per THRE seen, though
# QEMU's 16550 has working FIFOs; uart's Stats then report burst 1 (MR8).
# release.flood=32 makes root print, right after its summary, 32 numbered
# lines of 75 bytes with CR LF: 2,400 bytes, more than uart's 2,048-byte
# queue. The first is expected, the other 31 with next:, each whole, so
# nothing is lost or comes between them, and release's line comes right
# after the last. The run is otherwise release's: no kernel output, the
# probe's faults, the typed line read whole, and TEST PASS through
# isa-debug-exit. QEMU's transmitter takes each byte at once and raises
# THRE again, so one service routine empties the queue a byte at a time.
# release_burst15.scenario is the same with burst 15; the Hyper-V check
# runs both (tools/hyperv/m9-release-burst1.scenario, -burst15).
kernel: release
cmdline: test=release uart.burst=1 release.flood=32
exit: success
expect: loader: microL4 loader
expect: entering kernel
next: root: microL4 root task
expect: root: cmdline "test=release uart.burst=1 release.flood=32"
next: root: uart.burst=1: uart's burst capped at 1
expect: root: image frames: slots
expect: root: empty: slots
expect: release: flood 01/32 123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOP0
next: release: flood 02/32 23456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOP01
next: release: flood 03/32 3456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOP012
next: release: flood 04/32 456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOP0123
next: release: flood 05/32 56789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOP01234
next: release: flood 06/32 6789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOP012345
next: release: flood 07/32 789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOP0123456
next: release: flood 08/32 89abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOP01234567
next: release: flood 09/32 9abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOP012345678
next: release: flood 10/32 abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOP0123456789
next: release: flood 11/32 bcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOP0123456789a
next: release: flood 12/32 cdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOP0123456789ab
